for name in ('works','trenches','F1'):
 cases=exits['f1']['cases'] if name=='F1' else [c for c in exits['authored']['cases'] if c['key'].startswith(name)]
 n=len(cases);cells=[]
 for key in ('S','C','N','U','F120','F240'):
  cells.append('not gated' if name=='trenches' and key.startswith('F') else f\"{sum(c['checks'].get(key,False) for c in cases)}/{n}\")
 text+=f\"| {name} | \"+' | '.join(cells)+f\" | {sum(not c['adverse'] for c in cases)}/{n} |\\n\"
text+='''
Mean per-run metrics follow. Closure cells show mean (available n); unavailable horizons are excluded from means but **do not pass** the per-run criterion. This matters for F1's early decisions. See the complete paired distributions and2000 generated-map-cluster bootstrap95% CIs in [the family report](../phase2b/f1-report.md) and its JSON.

